`mkit serve` is only the ssh-frame stdin/stdout server. The HTTP and
mkit+enc:// listener flags it used to take are unknown arguments (usage
error, exit 64) with a pointer to `mkit-server`.

```
$ mkit serve --http 127.0.0.1:0 .
? 64
error: unexpected argument '--http' found

  tip: to pass '--http' as a value, use '-- --http'

Usage: mkit serve <PATH>

For more information, try '--help'.
hint: `mkit serve` no longer takes `--http`; it only speaks the ssh-frame protocol on stdin/stdout.
      The HTTP and mkit+enc:// listeners are the separate `mkit-server` binary:
        mkit-server serve --repo-root <PATH> --listen <ADDR>      (was: mkit serve <PATH> --http <ADDR>)
        mkit-server serve --repo-root <PATH> --listen-enc <ADDR>  (was: mkit serve <PATH> --listen-enc <ADDR>)
      See "Migrating from `mkit serve --http` and `--listen-enc`" in docs/CLI.md.

```

```
$ mkit serve . --listen-enc=127.0.0.1:9418 --unsafe-allow-any-enc-peer
? 64
error: unexpected argument '--listen-enc' found

  tip: to pass '--listen-enc' as a value, use '-- --listen-enc'

Usage: mkit serve <PATH>

For more information, try '--help'.
hint: `mkit serve` no longer takes `--listen-enc`; it only speaks the ssh-frame protocol on stdin/stdout.
      The HTTP and mkit+enc:// listeners are the separate `mkit-server` binary:
        mkit-server serve --repo-root <PATH> --listen <ADDR>      (was: mkit serve <PATH> --http <ADDR>)
        mkit-server serve --repo-root <PATH> --listen-enc <ADDR>  (was: mkit serve <PATH> --listen-enc <ADDR>)
      See "Migrating from `mkit serve --http` and `--listen-enc`" in docs/CLI.md.

```

An unrelated unknown flag gets clap's error alone.

```
$ mkit serve . --bogus
? 64
error: unexpected argument '--bogus' found

  tip: to pass '--bogus' as a value, use '-- --bogus'

Usage: mkit serve <PATH>

For more information, try '--help'.

```
